# Step 6: Review
## First line (every PR)
- Read Cursor Automations comments per `project-cursor-automations.mdc` (PR review, Find vulnerabilities, Bugbot; CI triage if CI was red).
- Green CI (build, tests, gitleaks). Formats and impersonal wording: `playbook-git-pr.mdc`.
- Docs-with-code: PR names the `Doc-` page to update, or «вики не затронута».

## Escalation (architect / designated reviewer)
Run a dedicated review (diff vs page «Архитектура» and «Тест-кейсы», plus security depth) when any of:
- an automation left a blocker or a validated finding;
- the PR is risky (auth, secrets, payments, infra, migrations, public API contracts);
- the diff is large or crosses services;
- the Feature/Epic page changed in «Архитектура» or «Решения» for this work;
- the lead or owner asks for a human/architect pass.

Otherwise the lead may merge on automations + green CI alone (bugs/small fixes and routine cloud-agent PRs).

## Verdict
- Page mismatch: changes requested, or a «Решения» row if the page is wrong.
- Architect verdict: GitHub review, Russian, comment template. Server-side security for risky infra still needs a person with server access (lead), not only the automation comments.
